    rdfs:label "Dormant Commerce Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Dormant Commerce Clause claim is a legal argument asserting that a state law or regulation violates the United States Constitution by burdening or discriminating against interstate commerce. This claim is based on the interpretation that the Commerce Clause not only grants Congress the power to regulate commerce but also implies a limitation on state interference with interstate commerce." ;
