<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7PjSMSqDsr4pw5CY13gyBr> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Application for National Interest Waiver" ;
    rdfs:comment "In the United States, an application for National Interest Waiver (NIW) is a request submitted by foreign nationals seeking an exemption from the labor certification requirement as part of the employment-based green card process in the United States. By applying for an NIW, applicants are essentially requesting that the requirement for a job offer and labor certification be waived due to their work being deemed in the national interest of the United States. The NIW is typically filed as part of the I-140 petition (Immigrant Petition for Alien Worker) and requires demonstrating how the applicant's work benefits the U.S. in a significant and unique manner" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RKY2B2HNSx5K82dgVN6Qn7> ;
    skos:altLabel "EB-2 NIW",
        "Form I-140 NIW",
        "I-140 NIW Petition" .

