<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7qgJwhdyqvE8u175RN80fT> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Reprieve" ;
    rdfs:comment "A reprieve is a temporary delay or suspension of a punishment or sentence, especially in the context of the death penalty. It serves as a postponement of the execution of a sentence, often to allow the defendant more time to seek a new trial, appeal, or another form of relief. However, a reprieve does not change the underlying conviction or sentence; it only delays its enforcement." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCRVBAzI4EaLARuVLhgDBTB> .

