    rdfs:label "D.O. (Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine)" ;
    rdfs:comment "A D.O. (Doctor of Osteopathic Medicine) is a medical degree awarded after completing osteopathic medical school, emphasizing a holistic approach to healthcare. It signifies qualifications to practice medicine and perform surgery similar to M.D. (Doctor of Medicine) holders" ;
