    rdfs:comment "A Transit Visa to the United Nations is a specialized type of transit visa issued to individuals who need to pass through the United States en route to the United Nations headquarters in New York City for official UN business. This visa allows the holder to enter and transit through the U.S. solely for the purpose of conducting activities related to the United Nations and is generally valid for a limited period." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCuTj4Z7aSLh4BBpXWs0ci4> ;
    skos:altLabel "C-2 Visa" .

