    rdfs:comment "Fiscal Monopoly Profit Payment refers to the portion of profits generated by government-controlled monopolies that is transferred to the general government or used to finance government expenditures. These profits are considered part of government revenue and are recorded when they are either transferred to the government or used to cover government expenditures." ;
