    rdfs:label "Joint Guarantee" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Joint Guarantee is a financial arrangement where an entity other than the issuer, typically a corporation, provides an assurance to fulfill the obligations of a debt instrument if the primary obligor defaults. This type of guarantee creates a shared responsibility for the debt, with both the issuer and the guarantor being jointly liable for the repayment, thus enhancing the creditworthiness of the instrument." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RfuC0yNDKhOWj8FHvjuYyg> ;
