    rdfs:comment "Dyslexia is a specific learning disability that affects an individual's ability to read, spell, write, and sometimes speak, due to difficulties in recognizing and processing written words and symbols. It is a neurological condition that is often hereditary and varies in severity, requiring tailored educational strategies and interventions." ;
