    rdfs:label "Motion to Waive Credit Counseling" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Motion to Waive Credit Counseling is a formal request submitted by a debtor to a bankruptcy court to exempt them from the mandatory credit counseling requirement. This requirement is typically necessary before filing for bankruptcy, but the motion may be granted under special circumstances, such as exigency or incapacity." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9Ii4OzSADsjS0VegX12oQJ> .

