<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBzTYMdPGeM2JsutnZtT7Fi> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Outperformance Bonus Certificate" ;
    rdfs:comment "An Outperformance Bonus Certificate is a financial instrument that allows disproportionate participation in the positive performance of the underlying asset or assets above a certain strike level, combined with protective features. The minimum redemption value is equal to the nominal value, provided a specified barrier has not been breached; if the barrier is breached, the product converts into an outperformance certificate. With greater risk, multiple underlying assets (worst-of) allow for a higher bonus level or lower barrier, offering reduced risk compared to a direct investment in the underlying assets." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R2Kr3kWHR9cR4zALXqt1nM> .

