<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RC0zDBYjiRDO2hTdbUIcdhN> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Grand Jury Clause Claim" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Grand Jury Clause claim is a legal assertion that an individual's Fifth Amendment rights have been violated. In the United States Constitution, the Grand Jury Clause of the Fifth Amendment requires that a grand jury indictment or presentment be obtained before a person can be charged with a serious federal crime. A claim related to this clause may arise if an individual believes that their case was not properly or fairly considered by a grand jury, or if the grand jury proceedings were flawed in some significant way." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCvD6VheGrBYqJhgQDfMbrV> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf die Grand Jury-Klausel",
