<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCGquLtBt00CMIRpIU9jQqB> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Involuntary Commitment to a Mental Health Facility" ;
    rdfs:comment "Involuntary commitment to a mental health facility is a legal process where an individual is mandated to be admitted to a psychiatric hospital or clinic against their will. This typically occurs when the individual poses a significant risk to themselves or others due to a mental disorder, and the decision is often based on medical evaluations and established legal criteria." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDmZbwmBBKWQ3vGof1sh1kB> .

