    rdfs:comment "Overtime pay refers to the additional compensation provided to employees who work hours in excess of what is considered standard or regular for a given period, typically a workweek. The rate for overtime pay is often higher than the employee's regular hourly wage, commonly set at one and a half times the standard rate or more, depending on labor laws and employment contracts." ;
