    rdfs:label "Bordereau Matter" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Bordereau in legal contexts refers to a detailed note or memorandum listing various matters, such as documents or cases, often used in insurance and financial agreements to outline the specific details or items included within a contract or transaction. Insurance companies often provide these detailed reports to its reinsurers, outlining claims and premiums, helping track and manage reinsurance contracts and obligations." ;
