    rdfs:label "Data Protection Regulation" ;
    rdfs:comment "Data Protection Regulation refers to laws and policies designed to safeguard personal and sensitive information from unauthorized access, use, disclosure, alteration, and destruction. These regulations ensure that organizations (e.g., companies, nonprofits, governments) implement appropriate measures to protect data privacy and security, complying with legal standards such as the GDPR, CCPA, and HIPAA." ;
