<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDAQMAQLYgoUdaKQquAhteq> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Background Check" ;
    rdfs:comment "A background check is a process through which an individual's personal, criminal, credit, and/or employment history is investigated and verified, typically by an employer, landlord, or other decision-maker. Background checks are often conducted to assess an individual's suitability for employment, housing, or other opportunities, as well as to ensure the safety and security of a workplace or community. Common elements of a background check may include verifying identity, checking criminal records, reviewing credit history, confirming education and employment history, and examining professional licenses or certifications. In many jurisdictions, background checks are regulated by laws such as the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA) to protect individual privacy and prevent discrimination." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RdfKnWpXsG2eBmnS3oJNTF> ;
    skos:altLabel "Background Check",
        "Hintergrundüberprüfung",
        "Revisión de Antecedentes",
        "Verificación de Antecedentes",
        "Verificação de antecedentes",
        "Vérification des antécédents",
        "בדיקת רקע",
        "पृष्ठभूमि जाँच",
        "バックグラウンドチェック",
        "背景调查" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDAUrTR1DjCiZrektRxwzar> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Uniform Dispute Resolution Service Provider" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Uniform Dispute Resolution Service Provider (UDRSP) is an organization accredited by the Internet Corporation for Assigned Names and Numbers (ICANN) to administer dispute resolution proceedings for domain name disputes under the Uniform Domain-Name Dispute-Resolution Policy (UDRP). These providers facilitate the resolution of conflicts between domain name registrants and trademark owners over domain name registrations." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RC8gGTL4dazXLDWuElLZLjI> .

