    rdfs:label "Fair and True Reporting Privilege" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Fair and True Reporting Privilege is a legal immunity and privilege that protects journalists and media outlets from being sued for defamation when reporting on matters of public interest, as long as they report accurately and in good faith." ;
