<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDZD8z35laaMMzT4c2ImnT4> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Change Management Risk" ;
    rdfs:comment "Change Management Risk refers to the potential for negative outcomes or disruptions when an organization undergoes transformations, such as implementing new processes, technology, or organizational structures. These risks may arise from poor planning, ineffective communication, resistance to change, or inadequate training, ultimately impacting employee morale, productivity, and the overall success of the change initiative" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RxTxaN981tLTsN82qPBcp> ;
    skos:altLabel "Organizational Transformation Risk" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDZJLfOjb6fGWxLAccPjKCr> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Vegetative State" ;
    rdfs:comment "A vegetative state is a condition in which a person is awake but shows no signs of awareness or response to the environment. It is characterized by the presence of sleep-wake cycles without cognitive function, often resulting from severe brain injury. This concept involves complex issues related to medical decision-making, guardianship, and end-of-life care. Legal challenges may arise in determining the rights and best interests of individuals in a vegetative state, particularly regarding life-sustaining treatments and the recognition of advance directives." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBrSWvfPR3YZFl63qupzFML> ;
    skos:altLabel "Persistent Vegetative State",
        "Unresponsive Wakefulness Syndrome" .

