    rdfs:comment "Auditability refers to the ability of an AI system to undergo an assessment of its algorithms, data, and design processes to determine whether the system is functioning as intended. Auditability does not necessarily imply that information about business models and intellectual property must always be openly available, but ensuring traceability and logging mechanisms from the early design phase can help enable the system's auditability" ;
