    rdfs:label "Death Certificate" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Death Certificate is an official document issued by a government authority that records the details of a person's death. It typically includes information such as the deceased individual's name, date and place of death, cause of death, and the attending physician's or coroner's signature. Death certificates are important for legal and administrative purposes, including the settlement of the deceased person's estate and handling matters related to inheritance, insurance, and funeral arrangements." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBCzyIAi2Hjl80hfQr8wAMR> .

