<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RVqw56uVNOkyhXBm2PRjJr> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Successor in Interest Petition" ;
    rdfs:comment "The I-140 Successor in Interest Petition is a process in the United States through which a new employer or entity assumes the sponsorship of an employment-based immigrant visa (green card) petition that was previously filed by a predecessor employer. This is relevant when the original petitioner goes out of business or undergoes a merger, acquisition, or other organizational change. The new employer or entity can file a Successor in Interest Petition to continue the green card process for the beneficiary (foreign worker) without starting the process anew, provided certain conditions are met." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RKY2B2HNSx5K82dgVN6Qn7> ;
    skos:altLabel "I-140 Successor in Interest Petition" .

