    rdfs:label "Huntington's Disease" ;
    rdfs:comment "Huntington's disease is a progressive neurodegenerative disorder characterized by the gradual onset of motor dysfunction, cognitive decline, and psychiatric symptoms due to the degeneration of neurons in the basal ganglia. It is caused by a genetic mutation in the HTT gene, leading to a typical onset in middle adulthood and requiring ongoing medical and supportive care." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RkvRD1NfpM4aO12DEEarGf> ;
