<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RqiDHswc43JoKvLEHWMGvR> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Prevailing Wage Violation Claim" ;
    rdfs:comment "A prevailing wage violation claim is a legal action initiated by an employee against their employer for not paying the required prevailing wage for work performed on a government-funded construction project or a project subject to prevailing wage laws. Prevailing wage laws require contractors and subcontractors to pay workers on public works projects the prevailing wage rate for their job classification in the local area where the work is performed. The claim typically arises when an employer pays workers less than the applicable prevailing wage rate or does not properly classify workers for the purposes of determining their prevailing wage rate." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9UYGSnWQz2MvNsWUofGb6J> ;
    skos:altLabel "Anspruch auf Verletzung des vorherrschenden Lohns",
