<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/Rt7y5QJoXmShB4OEPQ8Ysl> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Nutrition Market Segment" ;
    rdfs:comment "The nutrition market segment refers to a division of the market that is specifically targeted towards consumers who are interested in dietary and nutritional health. This segment encompasses products, services, and marketing strategies that are designed to cater to the needs, preferences, and interests of individuals who seek to maintain or improve their health through balanced and healthy eating habits, dietary supplements, and nutrition-focused products." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBXoCwCeY64Ow60nWKSZCC> .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RtLCzYWZfRT3o7tzhyamNE> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Peripheral Neuropathy" ;
    rdfs:comment "Peripheral neuropathy refers to a range of disorders caused by damage to the peripheral nerves, which are the nerves outside the brain and spinal cord. This condition often results in symptoms such as pain, numbness, tingling, and weakness, typically affecting the extremities like the hands and feet." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7M8wW11LJaLtWjQS7DmTQH> ;
    skos:altLabel "Peripheral Nerve Disorder" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RtSnrf1URIhJNP0fCJ6SZ7> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Mammals" ;
    rdfs:comment "Mammals are a class of vertebrate animals characterized by the presence of mammary glands which produce milk for feeding their young, hair or fur, and a neocortex region in the brain. Mammals are warm-blooded and include a wide range of species from terrestrial to aquatic environments, such as humans, elephants, and whales." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8sd4v04cEXnzbttN2gUEpV> .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RuFYyZorYWUSsV5u02JBYb> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Motion to Avoid Lien" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Motion to Avoid Lien is a legal request made in a bankruptcy case to remove a creditor's lien on a debtor's property, allowing the debtor to keep the property free and clear of the creditor's claim." ;
