    rdfs:comment "Zoological Taxonomy is the scientific classification of animals based on their evolutionary relationships, anatomical structures, and genetic similarities, organizing them into hierarchical categories such as phyla, classes, orders, families, genera, and species. This system helps in understanding the diversity of animal life and their biological characteristics." ;
