<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8AUKvbXRK8jOHSQaqxcAtD> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Legal Determination" ;
    rdfs:comment "\"Litigation determination\" refers to the final outcome or verdict reached in a legal dispute or trial. It can include findings such as \"guilty\" in a criminal case or \"liable\" in a civil case when a party is held responsible, or \"acquitted\" when a defendant is found not guilty in a criminal trial. A single matter's legal determination can be split between claims (e.g., liable for one claim; not liable for another claim)." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBDhSx7fl9qS0ezDVJuZHX4> .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8GqVQ7wf48MBB7IuqjSfOk> a owl:Class ;
