<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9SAKPHWeGi7uZqUG6EMlt> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Correctional Facility Official" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Prison Official is an individual responsible for the management, oversight, and operation of a correctional facility, ensuring security, order, and compliance with regulations. These officials oversee the staff, inmate population, and administrative functions, playing a critical role in maintaining the safety and rehabilitation efforts within the prison." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RCEDL3kMYgjFUEOhOyGp3IE> ;
    skos:altLabel "Correctional Facility Staff",
        "Jail Official" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9Sn2rwvFp1q6oYORzblWjv> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Winner-Take-All Electoral System" ;
    rdfs:comment "A winner-take-all electoral system is a voting method in which the candidate or party receiving the most votes wins all available seats or electoral votes, without any proportional distribution. This system is often used in single-member districts and can lead to a significant advantage for the majority party, potentially underrepresenting minority groups." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7OQ65vKuOBSSGgSVYnoMfx> ;
    skos:altLabel "Dominance Voting System",
        "Majoritarian System",
        "Plurality System",
        "Relative Majority System",
        "Simple Majority System",
        "Single-Member Plurality" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9UmIB7M3FM4ZjzKbv8zbId> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Zoning Document Amendments" ;
    rdfs:comment "Zoning Document Amendments pertain to the formal changes made to official zoning documents such as zoning maps and zoning ordinance text. These amendments can be initiated by private individuals, developers, or government bodies and usually require a comprehensive legal and regulatory review process, often including public hearings and official approvals." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RLIW6W1ctClGqwD8mjbMeQ> ;
    skos:altLabel "Zoning Code Modifications" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9Uol8M7H5u6lSDwss6uXIF> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Dementia" ;
    rdfs:comment "Dementia is a broad category of brain diseases characterized by a decline in memory, thinking, behavior, and the ability to perform everyday activities. It is a progressive condition that often leads to significant impairment in social and occupational functioning, requiring comprehensive medical and supportive care." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/REFNhmFYG6yk3W0RPLFV6g> ;
    skos:altLabel "Cognitive Decline Disorder" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9VP28VqK4AHUw790wby7ME> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Significant Shareholder Disclosure" ;
    rdfs:comment "Significant Shareholder Disclosure is an investor's filing with the financial regulator (e.g., U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)), providing detailed information about the investor's identity, background, source of funds, and intentions regarding the company, serving as a transparency measure to inform the market and the company's management. It's often triggered by an ownership threshold." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RmCERXtzdqIJcW9mdbk0Bb> .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9VgIGcn57gilWLqtXc5cNb> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Class" ;
    rdfs:comment "All those persons in the same category, level of rights (e.g. heirs of dead person who are related by the same degree), or who were injured by the same incident (e.g., class action lawsuit). Whether a person is part of a class often determines who can sue on behalf of the people who have been similarly damaged or collect his/her share if a class action judgment is entered." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8xoAbLw9cOhM7q4iRXRmXu> ;
    skos:altLabel "CLASS",
        "Class",
        "Classe",
        "Klasse",
        "クラス",
        "类" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9XzhwCpeRMiamNWRROfb75> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Meeting" ;
    rdfs:comment "A meeting is a type of communication event where individuals come together to discuss a specific topic or agenda." ;
