<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9g0tsF68ZfL1dvdj4jdg1t> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Contractual Standardization" ;
    rdfs:comment "Contractual Standardization refers to the extent to which the terms of a contract are standardized or custom-tailored. Standardized contracts have predefined terms and conditions that are universally applied, facilitating easier trading and regulatory compliance, while non-standardized contracts are customized to meet specific needs of the contracting parties." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R70jMZb6xYrVCXW6f3EbO1e> .

