    rdfs:comment "A State Government Representative is an elected or appointed official who serves in the government of a state, province, or similar sub-national administrative division. This individual is responsible for participating in the creation, debate, or implementation of state-level laws, policies, and programs, as well as representing the interests of their constituents within the state governmental structure." ;
