<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBi5nYq1khAzzGeY5YZ10ya> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Leave-Related Claims" ;
    rdfs:comment "Leave-related claims are legal actions initiated by an employee against their employer for not complying with applicable laws or the terms of an employment agreement regarding various types of leave, such as medical leave, family leave, or military leave. These claims can involve issues such as denial of leave, interference with the employee's right to take leave, or retaliation against the employee for taking leave. Employees may also bring leave-related claims if their employer fails to provide required notice or fails to provide benefits or protections required by law during the leave period." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8TmxqBbWaNgdm0lJQdY6D4> ;
    skos:altLabel "Ansprüche im Zusammenhang mit Urlaub",
        "Leave Claims",
        "Leave-Related Claims",
        "Reclamaciones relacionadas con licencias",
        "Reclamaciones relacionadas con permisos",
        "Reivindicações relacionadas a licenças",
        "Réclamations liées aux congés",
        "תביעות הקשורות לחופשה",
        "छुट्टी संबंधी दावे",
        "与休假有关的索赔",
        "休暇関連請求" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBkuFhzhFcv5vcQJU7NSntY> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Advance Directive" ;
    rdfs:comment "This is a broad term that refers to any document in which a person specifies what actions should be taken for their health if they are no longer able to make decisions for themselves because of illness or incapacity. An advance directive can include a variety of instructions about future medical care and can encompass several types of directives, including the living will and durable power of attorney for health care" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RB4GQZ26zq1PJ9m6vGUuoiy> .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBlWM6X0yqMrb4z4JQYaEP2> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "6th Amendment Claim" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Sixth Amendment claim is a legal assertion made by a defendant in a criminal case, arguing that their constitutional right to a fair trial, as guaranteed by the Sixth Amendment of the United States Constitution, has been violated. Such a claim may involve issues related to the right to counsel, the right to a speedy and public trial, the right to an impartial jury, or the right to be informed of the nature and cause of the accusation, among others." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R7MGQ9xUx0PxGLp5yxprdpZ> ;
    skos:altLabel "6 वीं संशोधन दावा",
        "6th Amendment Claim",
        "Anspruch auf den 6. Zusatzartikel",
        "Reclamo de la Sexta Enmienda",
        "Reivindicação da 6ª Emenda",
        "Réclamation au titre du 6ème amendement",
        "תביעת התיקון השישי",
        "第6修正案の主張",
        "第六修正案索赔" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBqTXginiTXVwXPwiLfOuDR> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "U.S. Patent Trial and Appeal Board" ;
    rdfs:comment "The U.S. Patent Trial and Appeal Board (PTAB) is a specialized administrative body within the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office (USPTO) that oversees post-grant review proceedings, inter partes review proceedings, and covered business method review proceedings." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RB8rNcS7dCmm3zkSaztNUz6> ;
    skos:altLabel "Conseil des recours des brevets des États-Unis",
        "Junta de Apelaciones y Juicios de Patentes de los Estados Unidos",
        "Junta de Pruebas y Apelaciones de Patentes de los Estados Unidos",
        "Junta de Recursos de Patentes dos EUA",
        "PTAB",
        "U.S. Patent Trial and Appeal Board",
        "ועדת המשפט וההתנגדות לפטנטים של ארצות הברית",
        "यूएस पेटेंट ट्रायल एंड एपील बोर्ड",
        "米国特許審判及び控訴委員会",
        "美国专利审判与上诉委员会" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBrSWvfPR3YZFl63qupzFML> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Neurological Collapse States" ;
    rdfs:comment "Neurological Collapse States refer to conditions characterized by severe impairment of brain function, leading to a significant reduction or absence of conscious awareness and neurological activity. These states can arise from various causes, including trauma, disease, or systemic failure, and are critical in determining legal and medical decisions regarding life support and end-of-life care." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RtHkyQ5lSxRaJ9oaSOWbkx> ;
    skos:altLabel "Severe Neurological Impairment States" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBt449Gy4YQBuVqNLxE7Gg> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Governmental Law Division" ;
    rdfs:comment "A Governmental Law Division is a legal entity within a government, responsible for providing legal services to government agencies, officials, and the public. It ensures legal compliance, represents the government in legal matters, and offers legal advice on policy and administrative issues." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RMIoMi1OqwHKqsjgrjdaHj> ;
    skos:altLabel "Government Legal Department" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBtf1nxagk3C03uC0micRM9> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Funeral Practices" ;
    rdfs:comment "Funeral Practices are the various rituals, ceremonies, and customs performed to honor and remember a deceased person. These practices vary greatly across different cultures, religions, and legal systems, often reflecting the beliefs and traditions of the community." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R8lhhP1c4Hm9RruhEpWMrJW> ;
    skos:altLabel "Funeral Rites",
        "Mortuary Practices" .

<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RBvtywUiDKBUTbufifIxsAh> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Deposition Posture" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deposition Posture refers to the specific role or position taken by a party during a deposition, such as observing, defending, or taking the deposition." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/RDrCoGiMIXR6TcVXppICUT5> ;
