<https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R4kWkG9m4DarQ45A7wBpJQ> a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Forensic Evidence" ;
    rdfs:comment "Forensic evidence pertains to scientific findings or techniques used in the criminal justice system to aid in the investigation and resolution of crimes. This evidence can encompass a wide range of disciplines, including DNA analysis, fingerprint identification, ballistics, toxicology, and digital forensics. Forensic experts analyze, interpret, and present this evidence in court to support or refute assertions made by parties in a case, ensuring its accuracy and reliability is crucial for just outcomes." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf <https://folio.openlegalstandard.org/R9HuNkpWm24qMFuntuug6RB> .

