    rdfs:label "Leguminous Vegetables" ;
    rdfs:comment "Leguminous vegetables, also known as legumes or pulses, are a category of vegetables from the legume family (Fabaceae), known for their pod-bearing growth habit and nutrient-rich seeds. They are consumed as a protein source in diets worldwide and are valued for their high protein, fiber, vitamin, and mineral content, as well as their role in improving soil fertility through nitrogen fixation." ;
